WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.400
[Instrumental music swells. A gold-lit globe turns.]
Heritage · Fellowship · Service

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:09.500
[The view descends towards Glasgow,
then into a gold outline of the city.]

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:15.400
A Robert Adam landmark in the Merchant City.
[Trades Hall assembles above the surrounding streets.]

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:19.400
[Columns, pediment and dome rise into place,
accompanied by mechanical clicks and impacts.]

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:24.800
A Robert Adam Masterpiece.
[The camera approaches the glowing gold facade.]

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:30.980
Opened in 1794.
[The camera passes through the entrance.]

00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:35.600
[A wood-panelled entrance hall and staircase.]
Still serving the purpose for which it was built.

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:39.600
[The view rises through the staircase,
past portraits and carved wooden balustrades.]

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:45.600
The Grand Hall. Heritage · Culture · Community.
[A chandelier hangs above the empty hall.]

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:50.500
What's Your Occasion? Weddings · Celebrations.
[Glowing floor-plan shapes spread across the room.]

00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:55.740
[Tables and chairs rise in gold outlines,
then transform into a dressed wedding reception.]

00:00:55.740 --> 00:01:02.430
Conferences · Meetings. Up to 250 guests.
[Rows of outlined chairs become theatre seating.]

00:01:02.430 --> 00:01:09.630
Private Dining.
[Long banquet tables appear, then become fully dressed.]

00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:16.030
Exhibitions · Markets.
[Display stands rise into a furnished exhibition layout.]

00:01:16.030 --> 00:01:22.800
Receptions.
[Standing tables and a reception layout fill the hall.]

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:27.000
[The camera tilts towards the painted ceiling
and central chandelier.]

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:31.800
Which Craft is yours? The 14 Incorporated Trades.
[Crests appear around a glowing ring; chimes sound.]

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:36.600
[The ceiling fades into a navy and gold title card.]
Trades Hall of Glasgow. Host here. Belong here.

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:40.200
One landmark. Every occasion. 85 Glassford Street · Glasgow.
Planned with Venviewer. [Music fades.]
